# the Arm architecture's floating-point arithmetic, which works on real numbers and the soft-float: the back end lowers
# each (tools/sailgen/README.md, "Lowered"), so only its val is copied
lower FPAdd
lower FPSub
lower FPMul
lower FPDiv
lower FPSqrt
lower FPMulAdd
lower FPMax
lower FPMin
lower FPMaxNum
lower FPMinNum
lower FPCompare
lower FPRoundInt
lower FPRoundIntN
lower FPToFixed
lower FixedToFP
lower FPConvert__1
lower FPToFixedJS
lower FPConvertBF__1
lower FPRoundingMode

# NX's fixups for floating point (nx.sail) in their place: the SIMD&FP registers are _V's elements and FPCR is the
# register as the CPU keeps it; FP is enabled at EL0; nothing merges without FEAT_AFP; and FPAbs and FPNeg unpack an
# operand only under FEAT_AFP, which no guest has
stop V_read
stop V_set
stop FPCR_read
stop CheckFPEnabled64
stop CheckFPAdvSIMDEnabled64
stop IsMerging
stop UsingAArch32
stop HaveFP16Ext
stop FPUnpack__1
